{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
{# temporal_fusion_transformer.py.j2 - Interpretable TFT (Lim et al. 2019) #}
{#                                                                         #}
{# Single-shot CLASSIFICATION adaptation of the Temporal Fusion           #}
{# Transformer over rolling feature-vector windows (not quantile          #}
{# multi-horizon forecasting - that needs a different task/label/eval).   #}
{#                                                                         #}
{# Pipeline (src.ml.blocks.TemporalFusionTransformer):                     #}
{#   window (B,W,F) -> per-timestep Variable Selection Network across the  #}
{#   F engineered features -> LSTM local-context encoder -> static         #}
{#   enrichment GRN -> Interpretable Multi-Head Attention over W -> pos    #}
{#   -wise GRN -> last-timestep representation -> classification head.     #}
{#                                                                         #}
{# Inherits model-agnostic verbose-logging + loss-surface emit from        #}
{# src.ml.shared.torch_logging so the dashboard renders grad-norm / lr /   #}
{# throughput / VRAM time-series, a filter-normalized 3D loss surface, and #}
{# TFT interpretability regardless of which model the user picked.         #}
{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
